<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria to offer 12 bln levs 3-mth T-bills Dec 2.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria to offer 12 bln levs 3-mth T-bills Dec 2.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry will offer 12 billion levs of three-month floater coupon T-bills at an auction on Monday, the central bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The issue will be offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry.</p>
<p>The coupon equals the BNB's central interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at 15 percent monthly or 180 percent annually.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow:</p>
<p> Issue number	 BG 3020696020</p>
<p> Auction date	 December 2, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date	   December 4, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date	March 5, 1997</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
